# Quadratic equation px^2 + qx + r = 0.
# Source: A. I. Kitov, N. A. Krinitsky, Elektronnye tsifrovye mashiny i programmirovanie (Electronic Digital Machines and Programming), 1959, docs/ecm_i_prog.pdf, section 31 example 2, printed pp. 156-157.
# The book gives the program in symbolic addresses with the allocation
# a=0020, h=0040, g=0045, b=0050, c=0054, d=0060, and leaves the substitution
# to the reader. This listing is that substitution.
# Book typo: the collected program on p. 157 prints h+1 as b+4 b+4 d+1 13.
# Step 4a on the same page gives opcode 05 (2 x 2 = 4, the complex-roots flag),
# which this listing uses at 0041.
# Answer: 0061 = 2 for real roots or 4 for complex roots; 0062, 0063 = x1, x2,
# or the real and imaginary parts. 0055-0060 are working cells.
# The book gives no input card for this example.
START 0020
0020 0051 0003 0051 0 72
0021 0051 0054 0055 0 05
0022 0055 0054 0056 0 05
0023 0056 0053 0056 0 05
0024 0055 0000 0055 0 62
0025 0000 0052 0057 0 03
0026 0052 0052 0060 0 05
0027 0060 0056 0056 0 03
0030 0000 0056 0000 0 01
0031 0032 0041 0000 0 20
0032 0054 0000 0061 0 13
0033 0056 0000 0056 0 63
0034 0057 0056 0060 0 03
0035 0060 0055 0062 0 05
0036 0057 0056 0060 0 01
0037 0060 0055 0063 0 05
0040 0046 0046 0000 0 20
0041 0054 0054 0061 0 05
0042 0000 0056 0056 0 03
0043 0056 0000 0056 0 63
0044 0057 0055 0062 0 05
0045 0056 0055 0063 0 05
0046 0061 0002 0061 0 70
0047 0061 0002 0000 0 44
0050 0000 0000 0000 0 40
# 0051: p. The book gives no value; enter it before running.
# 0052: q. The book gives no value; enter it before running.
# 0053: r. The book gives no value; enter it before running.
# 0054: the constant 2 = 2. BCD word computed for this listing.
0054 0400 0000 0000 0 01
